<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-New chief for South Australian super fund.</title>
<headline>RTRS-New chief for South Australian super fund.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South Australian Government said on Thursday that Lew Owens had been appointed chief executive officer of the State's Superannuation Funds Management Corporation, effective October 18 1996.</p>
<p>Treasurer Stephen Baker said Owens, now chief executive of the State's workers' compensation scheme, WorkCover, had strong strategic planning capabilities and an outstanding track record at WorkCover during a period of major change.</p>
<p>The Superannuation Funds Management Corporation manages around A$2.3 billion of State Government employees' superannuation funds.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
